Size the DSpark draft against the vocabulary the target samples from, not the
one it embeds. Apertus 1.5 embeds 266752 ids (text and media tokens) but its
LM head has 131072 rows (text_config.output_vocab_size). The e10 drafter
embeds the target's 266752 ids and drafts over the head's 131072, sharing
both from the target. Upstream compared the draft vocabulary with the
embedding size, called it reduced and refused to load (smoke job 3672166):

    ValueError: Reduced-vocabulary Qwen3 DSpark checkpoints must include
    lm_head weights; the full target lm_head cannot be shared.

The draft vocabulary (the d2t decision, the reduced-vocabulary check and LM
head sharing) is now compared with output_vocab_size when the target config
has one; the input vocabulary and embedding sharing still use the embedding
size (comparing those with the head size fails the other way, job 3672211).
Applies after vllm-apertus-dspark-mrv2-inner.

